    {
      "name": "Capuchin's Curse",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [
        "curse",
        "divine"
      ],
      "description": "<p>If a capuchin damages a creature with its jaws Strike, the creature gains both a blessing and a curse that last for 1d6 hours.</p>\n<p>While the blessing doubles the amount of time that the affected creature can hold its breath, the curse imposes a quickened version of the capuchin's moisture dependency, taking 1d6 damage every 10 minutes they go without water.</p>\n<p>A cursed creature can fully immerse itself in water as a 3-action activity to attempt a DC 17 Fortitude Saving Throw save, ending both the blessing and the curse on a success.</p>",
